{"slug": "temperature-classes-in-hazardous-areas", "question": "What Are Temperature Classes in Hazardous Areas?", "body_html": "<p style=\"margin:0 0 8px;\">Temperature classes in hazardous areas define the maximum surface temperature a device may reach, which must stay below the auto-ignition temperature of the gas or vapor present.</p><table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:8px 0 4px;font-size:16px;\"><tr style=\"background:#1a2b4a;color:#fff;\"><th style=\"padding:8px;text-align:left;\">Class</th><th style=\"padding:8px;text-align:left;\">Max surface temperature</th></tr><tr style=\"background:#eef4fb\"><td style=\"padding:8px;\">T1</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">450°C</td></tr><tr style=\"background:#fff\"><td style=\"padding:8px;\">T2</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">300°C</td></tr><tr style=\"background:#eef4fb\"><td style=\"padding:8px;\">T3</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">200°C</td></tr><tr style=\"background:#fff\"><td style=\"padding:8px;\">T4</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">135°C</td></tr><tr style=\"background:#eef4fb\"><td style=\"padding:8px;\">T5</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">100°C</td></tr><tr style=\"background:#fff\"><td style=\"padding:8px;\">T6</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">85°C</td></tr></table><p style=\"margin:0;\">A T4 device is not safe where T6 is required.</p>"}